==Combine==
{{main|NBA Draft Combine}}
The invitation-only [[NBA Draft Combine]] was held in Chicago from May 15 to 19. The on-court element of the combine took place on May 17 and 18. This year, 66 players were originally invited to the combine, including top prospects [[Zion Williamson]] and [[Ja Morant]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Zion Williamson Headlines 2019 NBA Draft Combine List of Invited Players|url=https://www.si.com/nba/2019/05/08/nba-draft-combine-players-invited-zion-williamson|date=May 8, 2019|website=si.com|access-date=May 12, 2019|archive-date=September 30, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200930070117/https://www.si.com/nba/2019/05/08/nba-draft-combine-players-invited-zion-williamson|url-status=live}}</ref> The pool of participants also included Croatian [[Luka Šamanić]], postgraduate [[Jalen Lecque]], and [[Darius Bazley]], who took a route similar to [[Mitchell Robinson]] with not playing in college or another league for a year before entering the draft. A couple of prospects also returned to the event after entering the previous year's combine, include an injury recovering [[Jontay Porter]] and [[Brian Bowen]], a player who entered last year as a collegiate participant last year before heading off to play professionally in [[National Basketball League (Australia)|Australia]] this year. In addition, this year also introduced the [[NBA G League]] Elite Camp, which gave a certain number of draft hopefuls a chance to transfer into the NBA Draft Combine afterward.<ref>{{cite web |title=80 players expected to attend 2019 NBA G League Elite Camp |url=https://pr.nba.com/2019-nba-gleague-elite-camp/ |website=NBA.com |access-date=May 18, 2019 |date=May 6, 2019 |archive-date=November 26, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201126104010/https://pr.nba.com/2019-nba-gleague-elite-camp/ |url-status=live }}</ref> This year, eleven participants from that event joined the combine, increasing the number of total invites up to 77.<ref>{{cite web |title=Sixty-six players expected to attend NBA Draft Combine |url=https://www.nba.com/article/2019/05/08/66-players-attend-nba-draft-combine |website=NBA.com |access-date=May 18, 2019 |date=May 8, 2019 |archive-date=August 10, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200810163703/https://www.nba.com/article/2019/05/08/66-players-attend-nba-draft-combine |url-status=live }}</ref> One of the additional invites was [[Tacko Fall]], who broke combine records for height (reaching {{height|ft=7|in=7}} with shoes on), wingspan, and standing reach.<ref>{{cite web |title=Tacko Fall headlines 2019 NBA Draft Combine measurements |url=https://www.nba.com/article/2019/05/16/nba-draft-combine-top-measurements-prospects |website=NBA.com |access-date=May 18, 2019 |date=May 16, 2019 |archive-date=May 16, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190516234241/https://www.nba.com/article/2019/05/16/nba-draft-combine-top-measurements-prospects |url-status=live }}</ref>

