The NBA draft lottery took place during the Playoffs on May 14, 2019. This was the first year in which the new NBA draft lottery system is applied, where the draft lottery was expanded to the top four picks (rather than the top three); and where the three teams with the worst records had equal odds. Teams with better records had an increased chance for a top-four pick when compared to the previous system, which was what happened for the [[New Orleans Pelicans]], [[Memphis Grizzlies]], and [[Los Angeles Lakers]] this year.<ref name="Draft lottery" />

